; Tags and links are not a transaction-only feature: beancount takes them on
; any directive line, and `#scanned` on a `document` is routine practice.
; They sit after the directive's own arguments and before its metadata.
;
; The parser used to read them only on transactions, so a line like the first
; one below matched no rule at all and disappeared down the catch-all.
2026-01-01 document Assets:Cash "statements/january.pdf" #scanned ^audit-2026
2026-01-02 note Assets:Cash "called the bank" #followup
2026-01-03 open Assets:Bank:Checking #new-account
2026-01-04 balance Assets:Cash 100.00 USD #reconciled
  source: "statement"
2026-01-05 close Assets:Bank:Checking ^migration
